  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 375.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Separate the egg whites from the yolks. Add Cream of Tartar to the whites and beat until soft peaks are achieved.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a food processor combine the egg yolks, 1/3 of the beaten egg whites, melted butter, almond flour, baking powder and salt (Adding approx. 6 drops of liquid sucralose to the batter can help reduce the mild egg taste). Mix until combined. This will be a lumpy thick dough until the whites are added.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the remaining 2/3 of the egg whites and gently process until fully incorporated. Be careful not to over mix as this is what gives the bread it's volume!",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour mixture into a buttered 8x4 loaf pan. Bake for 30 minutes. Check with a toothpick to ensure the bread is cooked through. Enjoy! 1 loaf makes 20 slices.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
